<title>GERMANY: GERMAN JAN-APRIL COFFEE IMPORTS UP FROM YEAR AGO.</title>
<headline>GERMAN JAN-APRIL COFFEE IMPORTS UP FROM YEAR AGO.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German net green coffee imports from outside the European Union totalled 4.55 million bags in January/April after 3.80 million in the same period last year, the DKV coffee industry association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The totals were rounded.</p>
<p>April imports alone were 1,172,477 bags compared with 982,094 bags in March and versus 902,114 bags in April 1996.</p>
<p>Leading suppliers in April were listed in the following order -- Brazil 261,580 bags (151,122 in March), Colombia 173,591 (190,651), El Salvador 168,295 (125,081), Vietnam 120,272 (85,600) and Uganda 69,761 (56,097).</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
